WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.479 --> 00:00:07.740
Somewhat literally, us humans are split right
down the middle, divided by the dichotomy

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.389
of our own nature.

00:00:09.389 --> 00:00:14.909
On the left side, our brain generally operates
out of reason and logic.

00:00:14.909 --> 00:00:20.880
And on the right, it generally operates out
of emotion and feeling.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:27.109
Both sides work for their cause and typically,
depending on the brain and the situation,

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:30.039
both sides can work together.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:36.180
But what is most interesting and potentially
very problematic is when they do not.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.340
When both sides are unable to find common
ground, leaving us, the experiencers of our

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.890
brains, hopelessly confused and distressed.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:53.320
When working together, our logical brain rationalizes
our emotions and our emotional brain inspires

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.899
our logic.

00:00:54.899 --> 00:01:00.910
Often times this can be successful and create
great synergy.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:07.220
But other times, there seems to be no successful
bridging between the two.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:14.150
One example of this that can cause us to feel
a sense of deep confusion and alienation from

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:21.000
our self is when our emotions and feelings
become so layered and complex that they cannot

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.550
be rationalized with or successfully articulated
by the logical side of our brain.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.550
When we experience the paradox of feeling
two or more conflicting emotions at the same

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.550
time.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:36.400
As strange as it may seem, it is possible
to experience two very conflicting feelings

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.210
simultaneously.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:46.810
It is possible to feel both angry with someone
for saying something cruel to you but simultaneously

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.200
sad that they feel that way about you.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:57.390
It is possible to feel both excited about
a career opportunity but scared of it at the

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.750
same time.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:06.310
It is possible to feel both happy about an
amazing moment or memory but also sad that

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.879
it is or will soon be gone.

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:16.319
It is possible to love someone for being perfect
for you, but simultaneously hate them for

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:18.980
not loving you back.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:25.290
And each pairing creates its own separate
unique feeling, very different from the feeling

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.180
of their individual counterparts.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.340
It is like tasting a sweet and sour sauce.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:38.940
Although there are both sweet ingredients
and sour ingredients, the blended flavor is

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.209
really neither sweet nor sour.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:45.939
It is its own separate and unique flavor.

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:49.920
And the blending of our emotions works just
the same.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:56.349
Furthermore, it is possible to feel a mix
of several emotions that don’t really distil

00:02:56.349 --> 00:03:04.110
down to a this and a that, but rather an array
of pushes and pulls and ups and downs in every

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:12.109
which direction, creating a feeling of indescribable
numbness that can not even be pinpointed on

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:14.439
a reason for feeling it.

00:03:14.439 --> 00:03:22.430
A feeling of confusion, despair, or overwhelm
for no apparent reason.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:29.579
From a logical perspective, how is it possible
that we can feel two or more opposing emotions

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:31.550
at the same time?

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:36.999
Simply, it is because we can and because we
do.

00:03:36.999 --> 00:03:43.239
Life and our emotional experience of it is
not always black and white.

00:03:43.239 --> 00:03:47.700
And it is not always logically discernable.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:52.680
There are innumerable shades of emotional
grey area.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.409
Some that our logical eye can distinguish.

00:03:56.409 --> 00:03:58.439
Some that it cannot.

00:03:58.439 --> 00:04:03.540
And when we cannot discern or classify a feeling,
what do we do?

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:08.609
Quite naturally, we become confused and overwhelmed.

00:04:08.609 --> 00:04:15.329
Our ability to make decisions, changes, or
simply understand our self and feel normal

00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:18.040
all become impaired.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:25.350
But we must accept that despite how hard it
tries, our brain does not yet fully understand

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.850
itself, and therefore neither can we.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:36.730
As we continue to evolve and learn as a species,
perhaps we will be able to better understand

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:44.280
and define the depth of grey area that resides
between our left and right self.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:50.121
Perhaps we will better understand what we
feel, why we feel the things we feel, and

00:04:50.121 --> 00:04:54.120
how to better articulate and deal with them.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:05:00.240
But until then, we must acknowledge and accept
that there are things that we cannot control

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.480
or understand about our self, and as a result,
sometimes we are going to feel confused or

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.480
overwhelmed.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:17.240
Sometimes we are going to feel two or three
or however many emotions at once that may

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:22.140
seem as though they don’t make any sense
and cannot be sourced for meaning or reason.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.870
But we should not feel alone or abnormal because
of this.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.450
And we should not let it dishearten us.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:31.280
Instead, we should instruct our left-brain
to rationalize with the fact that the left-brain

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:35.770
simply cannot always rationalize with everything
we feel and experience in life.

